1
00:00:06,881 --> 00:00:09,971
(Sheldon:)Here's the problem with teleportation.

2
00:00:12,721 --> 00:00:14,641
(Leonard:)Lay it on me.

3
00:00:14,806 --> 00:00:16,596
Assuming a device could be invented...

4
00:00:16,766 --> 00:00:20,436
...which would identify the state of matter
of an individual in one location...

5
00:00:20,603 --> 00:00:23,443
...and transmit that to a distant location
for reassembly...

6
00:00:23,606 --> 00:00:25,856
...you wouldn't have
transported the individual...

7
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:31,156
(Sheldon:)...you would have destroyed him in one
location and re-created him in another.

8
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,370
(Leonard:)How about that.

9
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:36,790
(Sheldon:)I would never use a transporter.

10
00:00:36,953 --> 00:00:39,623
(Sheldon:)The original Sheldon
would have to be disintegrated...

11
00:00:39,789 --> 00:00:42,539
(Sheldon:)...in order to create a new Sheldon.

12
00:00:43,001 --> 00:00:47,091
(Leonard:)Would the new Sheldon be in any way
an improvement on the old Sheldon?

13
00:00:48,006 --> 00:00:50,296
(Sheldon:)No, he would be exactly the same.

14
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:52,347
(Leonard:)That is a problem.

15
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:53,760
So you see it too?

16
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:56,851
(Dr Gablehouser(arriving):)Dr. Hofstadter, Dr. Cooper.

17
00:00:57,015 --> 00:00:58,225
BOTH:
Dr. Gablehauser.

18
00:00:58,391 --> 00:01:00,771
(Gablehouser:)Gentlemen,
I'd like you to meet Dennis Kim.

19
00:01:00,935 --> 00:01:03,775
Dennis is a highly sought-after
doctoral candidate.

